WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.434
-It is time to play
a game of deception

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.601
called "True Confessions."

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:13.467
♪♪

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:17.000
My first opponent tonight is
a multitalented actor, writer,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.767
and comedian whose new HBO max
special "Marlon Wayans Presents:

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.501
The Headliners"
premieres tomorrow.

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:24.634
Please welcome Marlon Wayans!

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.067
Wow. Wow.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.601
You just kind of -- Wow!

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.334
-I'm going to win this one,
Jimmy.

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.634
-You just came right in. Looked
Like a magnet brought you in.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.000
-That's right 'cause
I'm here for business.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.901
I'm winning this one.
I've been on this show 17 times.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.534
I haven't won nothing.
This is rigged.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:47.434
-Marlon and I will be facing off
against an amazing actress

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:50.534
who's currently starring in
season two of "Russian Doll,"

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:52.567
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.133
Please welcome Natasha Lyonne!

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:59.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.868
Natasha Lyonne!

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.734
So good to see you.
-You too.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.100
-You look great.
Now, here's how this works.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.000
In front of each of us are
two envelopes

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.267
containing confessions.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.300
One is true. The other is a lie.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.601
Once you read your confession,

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.400
the other two players
get to interrogate you.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.467
Then we have to come to
a unanimous decision.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.133
Is it the truth or is it a lie?

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.000
Marlon, you'll go first.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.934
Which envelope should
Marlon open?

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:24.400
One or two?
-Sir?

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.934
-Yeah, what do you think?
-I get to choose?

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.501
-No, I think we'll choose.
Right?

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.100
-See, it's already rigged.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.167
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.501
What do you guys think?

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:33.300
What does the audience think?
[ Audience shouts "two" ]

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.934
Two. Everyone's saying two.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.667
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.467
-So crazy you think
you're going to win.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:41.267
-Yeah. It's interesting.
-I am going to win.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:46.534
I once told Tupac that he had
eyes like Snuffleupagus.

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.767
-There's no way, man.
There is no way.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:54.000
-There's no way that he could --
What year was this?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.567
-Oh, uh, this was in the '90s.

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.868
I remember we had baggy pants on

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:03.701
and, uh, he was still rhyming
like, "Hey, B, see me."

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.467
-Where were you guys?

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.133
-Um, we was -- Where were we?

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:12.334
-Yeah, when you were with Tupac.
-We was at Glam Slam

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.100
in Los Angeles.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.667
That was Prince's old club.
-I don't know, man.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.267
-Glam Salam?
-Glam Slam.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.601
-Oh, Glam Slam.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.868
-Was it like a tennis thing?
Like with also glamour?

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.567
Glam Slam?
-You know, Glam Slam.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.601
You know, Prince, he liked --
-Glam.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.601
-Yeah, glam and he liked slam.
-Now I understand.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.467
-So you were at Glam Slam,
which is like a club,

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:31.167
and you're sitting
next to Tupac.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:34.167
-Yeah, it was me, him,
and Biggie.

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:37.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.901
I got to put my glasses on.

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:40.734
-Yeah, yeah,
put your glasses on.

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.467
Wait, so you, Tupac, and Biggie
were sitting together,

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.534
and you lean over to Tupac
and you go,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.801
"Your eyes look like
Snuffleupagus"?

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.300
-How long are y'all gonna
ask me questions?

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.234
Yes, I told him --
-What was his reaction?

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.167
-I'm so sorry.
I have a follow-up question.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.834
What does that mean
when someone's eyes

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.567
look like Snuffleupagus?

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.000
-This is what the card says.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.734
I think because he had
very long eyelashes.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:09.534
-Oh, I see.
-Like Mr. Snuffleupagus.

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:10.901
And he also had
really soft hands.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:13.567
And I called him
the Palmolive Thug.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:14.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:16.834
-Did he go crazy?
Did he freak out?

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:18.167
Or was he laughing?

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.934
-And what was Biggie doing
this whole time?

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:23.133
-Biggie was just -- it was
all -- [ Snoring ]

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.367
He was just breathing.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:29.367
-I don't know 'cause Marlon --
I've seen him in action.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.000
He's a very popular guy,
very charming.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.634
-Oh, he is. He's a wonder.
-I could see him go to parties

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.734
and I could see him actually
saying to Tupac that and --

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:39.367
-And getting away with it.
-Yeah, and getting a laugh.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.801
Snuffleupagus-like
eyelashes but --

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.334
-And yet I think it's definitely
the truth.

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:45.968
No, I'm just kidding.
It's a lie. It's a lie.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.834
-We think it's a lie.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.801
-I got you, Jimmy!
It's the truth!

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:52.801
-What?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.834
-No way!

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.100
-Wow!
-What?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.434
-No way.

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:05.734
-Tupac and I did "Above the Rim"
together.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:10.033
I went to see Tupac and Biggie
perform at Glam Slam.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.767
We was all sitting around
cracking jokes,

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:14.634
and I told him he had eyes
like Mr. Snuffleupagus

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.701
'cause his eyelashes
were so long.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.701
-Yo, that is a great story.
You got us.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.434
Marlon Wayans, congratulations.
That's the way to do it.

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.167
-I won! I won!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.701
-No one ever --
First time you ever won.

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.200
No one ever wins.
-Do I get a prize?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.634
What do I get?
-Bragging rights.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.767
-This whole ashtray is yours.
-Yeah, you get the whole ashtray

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:34.100
of fake cigarettes burning.
Alright.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.267
It is my turn.
Which envelope should I open?

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:38.167
-One, baby, one, baby.
[ Audience shouts "one" ]

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.567
-Okay.
-One.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.100
-On Monday,
I was at the White House

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.367
and I helped the President
tie his tie.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:46.868
-Mm.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:51.334
Biden old. He need a little help
with them ties.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:52.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.701
-Alright, my first question is
when was Monday?

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.400
That's what's tripping me up
here.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.901
[ Laughter ]
-That's your first question?

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.267
Monday was this week.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:01.767
-Today is Wednesday.
-Today is Wednesday.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:02.834
-So let's start
at the beginning.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.167
-What time on Monday was this?

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.000
-I was there
for the Easter egg roll.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.167
I went with my wife and kids.
We went and I read a book.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.100
I didn't even know if I was
going to meet the President.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.133
Then I met him and yeah,
then I tied his tie.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.501
-Was he not wearing a tie?

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:18.334
Why were in his dressing
quarters?

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.267
-I wasn't in his dressing
quarters.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.467
I was actually in the Blue Room.

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:25.334
You have to go to the Green Room
to get to the Blue Room

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:26.634
to get a photo
with the President --

00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:28.267
-What happens? That's where
the President wears blue?

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:31.100
-What'd he smell like?
What'd he smell like?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.067
Was it cologne, dentures?
-Old Spice.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:34.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.868
-Old Spice. Okay.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.467
-No, no, no. He smelled great.
-Coffee breath?

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.734
-No coffee breath. He was there
with the First Lady.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.434
And I walked out.
I was kind of nervous.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:46.033
I was there with my kids.
He made a joke to my kids.

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.801
He said, "I don't know who your
dad is," something like that.

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:50.033
It was funny.
And then he stood up

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:53.534
and the First Lady said,
"Jimmy's tie looks great.

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.801
He always has nice ties
on his show."

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:58.033
And I go, that's 'cause I --
I go, "Thank you.

00:05:58.033 --> 00:06:00.167
That's 'cause I know
how to tie a knot.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:01.434
I know how to tie a good knot."

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.634
And he goes, "What's the
secret?" or something like that.

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:05.767
And I go, "I can tie yours."

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:07.834
-What kind of tie was --
Did you do a double knot?

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.300
A double Windsor?
What kind of tie --

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.501
-It's a flipover. I don't know.
-How many times you flip it?

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:16.734
-It's a two flip and then a push
through and a yank.

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:17.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:20.000
No, I gave a nice tie
and it worked.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.434
I couldn't believe
no one was stopping me

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.634
'cause I knew -- You don't
really see Secret Service

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:25.801
because they're kind of hiding.

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:26.901
But no one stopped me.

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.300
No one even said,
"Don't do that."

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.767
He's the one that loosened it
and took it all down.

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:33.100
And I'm like, "I'm gonna do
this," and I did it.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.334
I tied the President's tie.

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:36.133
And then he went
and spoke to America.

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:39.901
-I mean, I don't not believe it
is, the trouble here.

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:42.367
-He's Jimmy. He's going to --

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.367
I would let him
if I was the President.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:45.534
-If I wasn't the president.

00:06:45.534 --> 00:06:47.067
-Now, if I was Obama's tie --
Obama like,

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.334
"Nah, nah, get up on me.
We good, we good, bro."

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:51.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-But Biden, he may take the --

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:54.133
I'm gonna say it's real.
I'm gonna say it's true.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.934
-I think it's --
I think it's true.

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:57.100
Ah, it's gonna be a lie.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.334
-I got you. It's a lie.
-Damn!

00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:08.567
-Come on now!
I just made it up.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:10.167
I didn't know
what story to tell.

00:07:10.167 --> 00:07:12.100
They wouldn't let me touch the
President of the United States.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.868
-Why not?
-I didn't know.

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:16.100
It was Secret Service.
-Were you even there?

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.133
-No, I wasn't there.
No, I was there.

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:19.534
I was there.
-Oh, you were there.

00:07:19.534 --> 00:07:20.734
-I was at the White House
on Monday.

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:22.267
But I just figured it'd be
some type of story

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.267
that would happen to me.
-You're a good liar.

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:26.133
-Alright, Natasha,
it is now your turn.

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:27.133
-Thank you.
-Go for it.

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:29.133
-Which one?
-I think number one.

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:30.300
Number one.
[ Audience shouts "one" ]

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.901
-Alright, alright.
-I know it's season two

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:34.100
of "Russian Doll"
but number one, come on.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.367
-The first time I ever flew
on a plane,

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:40.067
Marlon Brando,
my close personal friend,

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:42.801
we worked together with
on "Scary Movie 2,"

00:07:42.801 --> 00:07:46.100
was in first class,
and he brought with him

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:50.667
an entire birthday cake to eat
on the plane.

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:53.667
-Did he share the cake?

00:07:53.667 --> 00:07:56.167
-He initially did not want to.

00:07:56.167 --> 00:07:57.167
I don't know if you know this,

00:07:57.167 --> 00:07:59.968
but Brando's birthday is
April 3rd.

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:01.567
I'm April 4th.

00:08:01.567 --> 00:08:07.067
So, you know, we would stay in
touch, and he would -- anyway --

00:08:07.067 --> 00:08:09.133
-Too many details already.

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:10.567
I feel like you're getting
a little nervous

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:12.033
and you're starting to give us
too much details.

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.501
We didn't ask
what birthday it was.

00:08:13.501 --> 00:08:15.968
-I just wanted you to know that
we have a similar birthday.

00:08:15.968 --> 00:08:17.601
-Where were you guys
on your way to?

00:08:17.601 --> 00:08:18.868
-Oh, yeah, good.

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:21.334
-He was on his way back
from Australia

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:24.067
because of [Laughs]
"The Island of Dr. Moreau."

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:26.567
I only laughed 'cause it's
your favorite movie.

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:28.234
-Yeah, I do like that movie.
Val Kilmer.

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:29.934
-That movie,
you're always texting.

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:32.334
-I always say I love
"Island of Dr. Moreau."

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:33.901
All the Marlon Brando --

00:08:33.901 --> 00:08:35.300
That and "Superman"
are my two favorites.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.901
-And I always say,
"What about 'Apocalypse Now?'

00:08:36.901 --> 00:08:38.701
and you always say,
"It's about Moreau, baby."

00:08:38.701 --> 00:08:39.968
-Yeah, it's about Moreau, baby.

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:42.033
So, you said he was flying back
from Australia.

00:08:42.033 --> 00:08:43.801
And you what? How are you --

00:08:43.801 --> 00:08:46.167
You greeted him in the plane
on your birthday?

00:08:46.167 --> 00:08:48.300
-I like flying, okay?

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.534 --> 00:08:51.434
-Wow, I think this is
off the rail.

00:08:51.434 --> 00:08:55.033
The question is, is Natasha
Lyonne playing us right now?

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:57.334
And purposely saying --
-Guys I just -- Marlon.

00:08:57.334 --> 00:09:00.801
I want you -- look at me.
-My name is Marlon, okay?

00:09:00.801 --> 00:09:02.968
So I'm trusting
my Marlon instinct.

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:05.200
I knew Brando too.
-We knew Brando.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.767
-Yes.
-I have those dailies.

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:08.834
-[ as Brando ]
Does he talk like this?

00:09:08.834 --> 00:09:12.501
-You knew him --
Y'all met on the set.

00:09:12.501 --> 00:09:13.901
-Did we? Did we?

00:09:13.901 --> 00:09:14.934
-[ Normal voice ] How did you
see him in first class?

00:09:14.934 --> 00:09:16.033
Were you in first class
as well?

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.334
-No.
-Oh, you don't think

00:09:17.334 --> 00:09:19.133
I travel first class?
-No, you do!

00:09:19.133 --> 00:09:22.334
Of course! Of course you do!
-Not back then. Not back then.

00:09:22.334 --> 00:09:26.801
-In '96 during the filming of
"The Island of Dr. Moreau"!

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:28.934
-Oh, okay. Well, maybe.

00:09:28.934 --> 00:09:30.200
-Wow!
-Was you in that movie?

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.334
-Wasn't I?
-You just look so young.

00:09:32.334 --> 00:09:34.033
-Thank you.
-Wait, so he got in.

00:09:34.033 --> 00:09:35.467
You said,
"Hey, Marlon, good to see you."

00:09:35.467 --> 00:09:38.434
And he goes [as Brando] "It's my
birthday, it's our birthdays.

00:09:38.434 --> 00:09:40.200
Would you like some cake?"

